# `actuarial::models::experience_change`

The rate change indicated by loss experience.

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series actuarial::models::experience_change(const pluss::Series &incurred_losses, const pluss::Series &exposure, const pluss::Series &current_premium, double fixed_expense, double variable_expense_ratio, double profit_ratio);
```

## What It Does

Runs the whole indication and returns only its last stage: the pure premium of each cell ([`premium_curve`](premium_curve.md)), the loaded premium ([`indicated_premium`](indicated_premium.md)) and the change from the current premium ([`rate_change`](rate_change.md)). It is the `rate_change` field of the [`PricingResult`](../pricing/PricingResult.md) of [`operators::price`](../pricing/price.md); use it when only the change is wanted, and the operator when the intermediate figures are too.

## Parameters

`incurred_losses`, `exposure`, `current_premium`
: Series of the same length: losses and exposure 0 or more, current premium strictly greater than 0.

`fixed_expense`, `variable_expense_ratio`, `profit_ratio`
: The loads, as for [`indicated_premium`](indicated_premium.md).

## Returns

A series of rate changes, one per cell.

## Errors

Throws the errors of [`operators::price`](../pricing/price.md): invalid loads when the operator is built and `premium_curve: …`, `rate_change: current_premium must be strictly > 0` for the data.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1: the rate change of each cell

Four cells with the standard loads.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series losses = pluss::make_series({520000.0, 690000.0, 810000.0, 1100000.0});
  const pluss::Series exposure = pluss::make_series({1000.0, 1200.0, 1500.0, 1800.0});
  const pluss::Series premium = pluss::make_series({700.0, 720.0, 740.0, 760.0});
  out.writeln(actuarial::models::experience_change(losses, exposure, premium, 50.0, 0.15, 0.05).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 2: the same as the step functions

Chaining the three functions gives the same figures.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  const pluss::Series losses = pluss::make_series({520000.0, 690000.0, 810000.0, 1100000.0});
  const pluss::Series exposure = pluss::make_series({1000.0, 1200.0, 1500.0, 1800.0});
  const pluss::Series premium = pluss::make_series({700.0, 720.0, 740.0, 760.0});
  const pluss::Series chained = actuarial::models::rate_change(premium, actuarial::models::indicated_premium(actuarial::models::premium_curve(losses, exposure), 50.0, 0.15, 0.05));
  out.writeln(chained.items<double>());
  out.writeln(actuarial::models::experience_change(losses, exposure, premium, 50.0, 0.15, 0.05).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 3: the same as the operator

The rate_change field of a pricing run.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series losses = pluss::make_series({520000.0, 690000.0, 810000.0, 1100000.0});
  const pluss::Series exposure = pluss::make_series({1000.0, 1200.0, 1500.0, 1800.0});
  const pluss::Series premium = pluss::make_series({700.0, 720.0, 740.0, 760.0});
  const actuarial::Experience experience{losses, exposure, premium};
  out.writeln(actuarial::operators::price(actuarial::Loads{50.0, 0.15, 0.05})(experience).rate_change.items<double>());
}
```

### Example 4: an unloaded indication

With no loads the change compares the pure premium with the premium.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series losses = pluss::make_series({520000.0, 690000.0, 810000.0, 1100000.0});
  const pluss::Series exposure = pluss::make_series({1000.0, 1200.0, 1500.0, 1800.0});
  const pluss::Series premium = pluss::make_series({700.0, 720.0, 740.0, 760.0});
  out.writeln(actuarial::models::experience_change(losses, exposure, premium, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 5: the errors

Invalid loads, a zero premium and mismatched lengths are refused.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::models::experience_change(pluss::make_series({1.0}), pluss::make_series({1.0}), pluss::make_series({1.0}), -1.0, 0.1, 0.1); });
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::models::experience_change(pluss::make_series({1.0}), pluss::make_series({1.0}), pluss::make_series({1.0}), 0.0, 0.6, 0.5); });
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::models::experience_change(pluss::make_series({1.0}), pluss::make_series({1.0}), pluss::make_series({0.0}), 0.0, 0.1, 0.1); });
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::models::experience_change(pluss::make_series({1.0, 2.0}), pluss::make_series({1.0}), pluss::make_series({1.0, 1.0}), 0.0, 0.1, 0.1); });
}
```

